1
00:00:00,920 --> 00:00:01,920
[gasps]

2
00:00:02,970 --> 00:00:04,340
How exciting.

3
00:00:04,430 --> 00:00:06,470
You're the one who will
be teaching me this book, yes?

4
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:09,810
[exclaims softly]

5
00:00:09,930 --> 00:00:12,480
[♪ opening theme song playing]

6
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:22,530
JAADUGAR

7
00:01:41,070 --> 00:01:42,610
[SORGHAGHTANI] Most incredible.

8
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:44,940
Now I have my very own copy
of Elements.

9
00:01:45,070 --> 00:01:46,190
OTCHIGIN

10
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:48,070
And Tolui found it, just for me.

11
00:01:49,780 --> 00:01:51,330
What is your name?

12
00:01:53,450 --> 00:01:55,750
Fatima, that is my name.

13
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:59,170
I help you in studies, Highness.
Happy to teach things.

14
00:01:59,500 --> 00:02:01,170
I can't wait.

15
00:02:01,290 --> 00:02:02,750
-[SITARA] Although...
-Hm?

16
00:02:02,880 --> 00:02:06,840
I feel confused.
Why is it Highness want book?

17
00:02:06,970 --> 00:02:08,630
It holds not much value.

18
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:09,680
[SORGHAGHTANI] Huh?

19
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:12,100
All it does is
just state obvious.

20
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:15,220
It says, "A point is that
which has no part."

21
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,690
And, "A line
is breadthless length."

22
00:02:17,810 --> 00:02:19,480
You see? It is useless.

23
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:22,480
Oh.

24
00:02:23,360 --> 00:02:24,530
[SITARA] I'm still not sure

25
00:02:24,690 --> 00:02:26,900
why she ever wanted the book
to begin with.

26
00:02:27,530 --> 00:02:28,610
But I could tell

27
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:31,990
the prince didn't have any idea
how valuable it really was.

28
00:02:32,830 --> 00:02:35,080
There's a chance
she might part ways with it

29
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,750
if she starts losing interest.

30
00:02:36,870 --> 00:02:39,120
It just states the obvious.

31
00:02:39,250 --> 00:02:41,210
Indeed it does. That's true.

32
00:02:41,330 --> 00:02:44,170
-At least for your people.
-[gasps]

33
00:02:44,290 --> 00:02:47,170
But for us, this book
represents something more,

34
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:48,800
and it's very special.

35
00:02:48,930 --> 00:02:50,470
By studying its pages,

36
00:02:50,590 --> 00:02:52,680
we will acquire
Western knowledge not found

37
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:54,390
-on the steppe.
-Huh?

38
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:58,220
Tolui is the Otchigin
and serves a crucial role.

39
00:02:58,980 --> 00:03:02,190
He's the keeper of the hearth,
watching over its fire.

40
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,940
Even after
his older brothers set off,

41
00:03:05,070 --> 00:03:06,780
and received their own pastures,

42
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:10,070
as the youngest son,
he remains in the household,

43
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:13,030
guarding the family fortune
he'll inherit one day.

44
00:03:13,490 --> 00:03:15,490
And because he's the Otchigin,

45
00:03:15,620 --> 00:03:17,240
my husband
will become the emperor.

46
00:03:18,120 --> 00:03:20,910
That said, he isn't exactly
what you might call

47
00:03:21,040 --> 00:03:22,170
the brightest at times.

48
00:03:22,290 --> 00:03:24,380
-[kids laughing]
-But it's not just him.

49
00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:26,340
Many of our people
are the same way.

50
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:29,300
They know only of life
out here on the steppe.

51
00:03:30,300 --> 00:03:33,300
Vast as it may be,
the world is vaster still,

52
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:36,010
and I wish to learn more...

53
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:38,350
about the lands within reach
of Mongol hooves

54
00:03:38,470 --> 00:03:40,140
and the ones even farther.

55
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,560
I've heard
that your people have been able

56
00:03:42,690 --> 00:03:43,810
to successfully
predict the movement

57
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:45,690
of the stars since antiquity.

58
00:03:46,650 --> 00:03:47,940
How curious!

59
00:03:48,190 --> 00:03:50,650
To think that you're able
to figure out the Earth's size!

60
00:03:51,990 --> 00:03:53,570
Are you saying
this person traveled

61
00:03:53,700 --> 00:03:54,870
to the ends of the Earth?

62
00:03:54,990 --> 00:03:57,780
Of course not.
He just used geometry.

63
00:03:57,910 --> 00:03:59,540
You know what makes
obvious things

64
00:03:59,660 --> 00:04:00,580
seem more obvious?

65
00:04:00,710 --> 00:04:03,120
We prove
all universal principles

66
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:05,920
after amassing examples
one by one.

67
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:10,550
I must gain knowledge for all
of our future generations.

68
00:04:11,420 --> 00:04:12,720
As I see it,

69
00:04:12,930 --> 00:04:15,720
that is the role of someone
who will be empress one day.

70
00:04:15,850 --> 00:04:17,100
[Sitara gasps softly]

71
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:24,060
[SITARA] Oh, why is it...

72
00:04:24,190 --> 00:04:26,190
why is it that she...

73
00:04:27,730 --> 00:04:30,360
Why does she infuriate me so?

74
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:32,570
Do you even have
the faintest idea

75
00:04:32,690 --> 00:04:34,990
how that book ended up
in your hands?

76
00:04:35,570 --> 00:04:36,910
Do you think you can imagine

77
00:04:37,030 --> 00:04:38,870
the misery and anguish
we must endure

78
00:04:38,990 --> 00:04:41,290
when thanking those
who robbed us of everything

79
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:43,040
for the charity you now offer?

80
00:04:44,460 --> 00:04:46,750
Do you know nothing
of how I truly feel

81
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:49,000
as I'm being forced
to sit here at your feet?

82
00:04:49,750 --> 00:04:52,460
Something wrong? I hope
you aren't feeling unwell.

83
00:04:53,470 --> 00:04:54,880
[Sitara cries softly]

84
00:04:55,010 --> 00:04:56,840
No, I admire you.

85
00:04:56,970 --> 00:04:58,470
[Sorghaghtani chuckles softly]

86
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:01,100
A great pleasure
to serve Highness.

87
00:05:01,220 --> 00:05:03,180
I work hard, I swear.

88
00:05:03,890 --> 00:05:06,850
I'm grateful to have your help,
so thank you.

89
00:05:07,230 --> 00:05:09,940
I know you must be tired.
You may rest now.

90
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:12,900
I excuse myself.

91
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,160
[Sitara grunts]

92
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:20,870
Such wisdom as yours

93
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:23,160
is something
our people desperately need.

94
00:05:23,580 --> 00:05:26,460
[SITARA] I feel ashamed
for wavering back then,

95
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:28,500
if only for even a moment.

96
00:05:30,130 --> 00:05:31,460
But now...

97
00:05:35,090 --> 00:05:39,430
I mustn't allow myself
to forget this anger inside.

98
00:05:39,550 --> 00:05:42,560
I will never yield...
to that woman.

99
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:46,060
[wind blowing]

100
00:06:04,790 --> 00:06:06,450
Oh, welcome back, Fatima.

101
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:08,580
I thank you
for venturing out here

102
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:10,250
even in this sandstorm.

103
00:06:10,630 --> 00:06:11,790
You're welcome.

104
00:06:12,500 --> 00:06:15,420
Here in Mongolia,
once the sandstorms have passed,

105
00:06:15,550 --> 00:06:17,010
spring will soon follow.

106
00:06:17,130 --> 00:06:19,720
How I miss Persia
in the springtime.

107
00:06:20,430 --> 00:06:23,680
My mother still has
not adjusted well to life here.

108
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:24,930
[Sitara sighs softly]

109
00:06:27,190 --> 00:06:29,020
-[KHESHIG] Fatima.
-[SITARA] Hm?

110
00:06:29,140 --> 00:06:31,650
[KHESHIG] Princess Sorghaghtani
is asking for you.

111
00:06:31,770 --> 00:06:33,940
She'd like
to begin her studies now.

112
00:06:35,820 --> 00:06:37,400
I would be happy to.

113
00:06:37,530 --> 00:06:39,950
♪

114
00:06:50,670 --> 00:06:51,790
[Sitara grunts]

115
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:54,920
-[barking]
-[Sitara groans]

116
00:06:55,050 --> 00:06:57,510
Look at your face.
What happened to you?

117
00:06:58,090 --> 00:07:01,010
There are far too many animals
in Mongolia.

118
00:07:01,340 --> 00:07:03,760
And they're nothing
but a big nuisance.

119
00:07:03,890 --> 00:07:05,470
Perhaps so.

120
00:07:06,010 --> 00:07:08,940
But once you get to know them,
they can be rather charming.

121
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:11,900
Can they now?

122
00:07:15,320 --> 00:07:16,980
[grunting]

123
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:23,780
Uh... [sighs]

124
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:26,450
♪

125
00:07:33,290 --> 00:07:34,830
[WOMAN 1] Here you go.

126
00:07:35,090 --> 00:07:36,750
Now just a moment.

127
00:07:37,170 --> 00:07:39,670
It's already
our second winter here.

128
00:07:40,010 --> 00:07:42,430
It appears that your health
is improving, Mother.

129
00:07:42,550 --> 00:07:46,220
[WOMAN 2] Well, I've finally
gotten used to life in Mongolia.

130
00:07:46,470 --> 00:07:47,510
[WOMAN 3] I don't think

131
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:49,890
I'll ever get used
to this cold weather.

132
00:07:54,230 --> 00:07:55,650
[Sitara whistles]

133
00:07:56,690 --> 00:07:58,320
[sheep bleating]

134
00:07:58,440 --> 00:07:59,740
Tchou, tchou!

135
00:08:03,320 --> 00:08:05,070
SUMMER, A.D. 1224

136
00:08:05,740 --> 00:08:07,330
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Three years had passed

137
00:08:07,450 --> 00:08:11,000
after Sitara became
Princess Sorghaghtani's tutor.

138
00:08:12,040 --> 00:08:15,250
The Mongol army defeated
the Shah of the Khwarazm,

139
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:17,880
a major power in Central Asia,

140
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:21,510
and returned in triumph to
their home camp on the steppe.

141
00:08:22,510 --> 00:08:23,970
To welcome them back,

142
00:08:24,090 --> 00:08:26,180
Sorghaghtani and the members
of her court

143
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:29,010
traveled southwest
of the Altai Mountains

144
00:08:29,140 --> 00:08:30,600
to the basin of the Emil River,

145
00:08:31,100 --> 00:08:34,310
where they feasted and hunted
to celebrate their victory.

146
00:08:35,690 --> 00:08:37,770
[HULEGU] Hey, Father!

147
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:39,900
[TOLUI] Hulegu! Kublai!

148
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:41,780
I took down this deer by myself.

149
00:08:41,900 --> 00:08:43,740
And I brought back a hare.

150
00:08:44,070 --> 00:08:46,200
[TOLUI]
You two take after your father.

151
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:47,910
[HULEGU] Did you see?

152
00:08:48,030 --> 00:08:50,080
This was my first time
to go on a hunt.

153
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,660
-Aren't I so amazing?
-[laughter]

154
00:08:51,790 --> 00:08:55,040
You truly are amazing. [laughs]

155
00:08:55,290 --> 00:08:57,290
Prince Hulegu, Prince Kublai,

156
00:08:58,090 --> 00:09:00,670
the Great Khan will be
arriving here very soon.

157
00:09:00,800 --> 00:09:01,880
Please get ready.

158
00:09:02,010 --> 00:09:04,010
Fatima, see that? Look!

159
00:09:04,130 --> 00:09:07,090
My! That is truly
a splendid deer.

160
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:10,010
And taking down a nimble hare
is quite impressive as well,

161
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:11,140
Prince Kublai.

162
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:12,430
[Kublai chuckles]

163
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:15,440
Thanks. I guess
all my practicing has paid off.

164
00:09:15,850 --> 00:09:17,440
Who is that girl there?

165
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:19,770
She's the tutor
who helps me read Elements,

166
00:09:19,900 --> 00:09:21,480
the one you went
and found for me.

167
00:09:21,610 --> 00:09:23,900
Oh, yes,
she's the scholar's daughter.

168
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:26,700
Is she performing
her duties well?

169
00:09:26,820 --> 00:09:28,740
[SORGHAGHTANI]
I find her to be quite diligent,

170
00:09:28,870 --> 00:09:30,620
-clever, and thoughtful.
-[laughter]

171
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,620
And when I see her smiling
so fetchingly,

172
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:35,710
I am reminded how young she is.

173
00:09:36,290 --> 00:09:38,040
First,
you brought me Elements,

174
00:09:38,170 --> 00:09:39,630
then a remarkable tutor.

175
00:09:39,750 --> 00:09:41,550
Why yes, of course.

176
00:09:41,670 --> 00:09:43,670
-[HULEGU] Don't I look dashing?
-[laughs]

177
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,010
-[Hulegu grunts]
-And powerful too.

178
00:09:45,130 --> 00:09:48,220
You do know, it is a tradition
after your first hunt

179
00:09:48,340 --> 00:09:50,970
to have the animal's fat rubbed
on your fingers,

180
00:09:51,100 --> 00:09:53,390
and the Great Khan
will do the honors.

181
00:09:53,520 --> 00:09:55,600
[LADY-IN-WAITING]
The Great Khan has arrived.

182
00:09:55,730 --> 00:09:57,890
-[HULEGU] Come on, let's go!
-[KUBLAI] Yeah.

183
00:09:58,020 --> 00:10:00,360
[boys laugh]

184
00:10:03,780 --> 00:10:04,820
[gasps]

185
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:06,820
♪

186
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:11,780
[SITARA (ADULT)] The emperor
of the Mongols, Genghis Khan.

187
00:10:12,910 --> 00:10:16,120
It was he who established
this mammoth empire.

188
00:10:16,710 --> 00:10:18,540
In only three years' time,

189
00:10:18,670 --> 00:10:22,000
the fates written in the stars
of those who were present here

190
00:10:22,130 --> 00:10:25,670
would be set into grand motion
and forever changed

191
00:10:25,800 --> 00:10:28,300
after his inevitable fall.

192
00:10:33,180 --> 00:10:35,010
[wind blowing]

193
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:50,410
SUMMER, A.D. 1227

194
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:57,660
[TOLUI]
Great Khan... rest assured...

195
00:10:57,870 --> 00:11:02,340
the future of the Mongols
shall be just as you willed it.

196
00:11:04,340 --> 00:11:06,250
Father... [grunts]

197
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:07,800
♪

198
00:11:28,990 --> 00:11:31,200
[SITARA (ADULT)]
The fourth prince, Tolui,

199
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:33,490
as the youngest brother,
and Otchigin,

200
00:11:33,620 --> 00:11:35,910
maintained their custom
of ultimogeniture

201
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:39,160
and inherited the vast majority
of his father,

202
00:11:39,290 --> 00:11:40,960
Genghis Khan's legacy.

203
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:43,250
In addition to land and fortune,

204
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:45,250
Tolui's family came to control

205
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:48,130
almost all
of the imperial Mongol military

206
00:11:48,250 --> 00:11:49,920
and its divisions.

207
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:53,050
♪

208
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:01,180
[excited chatter]

209
00:12:04,980 --> 00:12:06,230
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Following the death

210
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:09,070
of Genghis Khan,
the empire needed to choose

211
00:12:09,190 --> 00:12:10,900
who would be its new ruler.

212
00:12:12,280 --> 00:12:14,990
But the tribal council known
as a Kurultai,

213
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:17,580
where the imperial clan
and contending princes

214
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:19,620
gather to elect a new emperor,

215
00:12:19,750 --> 00:12:22,540
wouldn't be convening
for another two years.

216
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:24,420
During this time,

217
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:26,710
Tolui didn't just
lead the military,

218
00:12:26,840 --> 00:12:30,340
but all state affairs
while acting as regent.

219
00:12:31,050 --> 00:12:35,760
AUTUMN, A.D. 1229

220
00:12:35,890 --> 00:12:38,850
Doesn't look to be
in the best of health, does it?

221
00:12:38,970 --> 00:12:42,850
That said, it should still be
safe to eat. Let's slaughter it.

222
00:12:44,810 --> 00:12:46,230
[sheep bleats]

223
00:12:50,530 --> 00:12:53,360
[sheep bleats]

224
00:12:57,450 --> 00:12:59,280
That should do it.

225
00:12:59,990 --> 00:13:02,370
Hey, keep on butchering away.

226
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:05,210
A massive feast like this one
is once in a lifetime.

227
00:13:06,710 --> 00:13:10,130
Here you are. Clean up
all these entrails for me.

228
00:13:12,050 --> 00:13:15,050
[SITARA] In the name of Allah,
and Allah is the greatest.

229
00:13:15,170 --> 00:13:17,550
Uh... Hey, Fatima.

230
00:13:17,970 --> 00:13:19,140
Hmm?

231
00:13:20,050 --> 00:13:23,180
What is it? Does cutting
into the abdomen bother you?

232
00:13:23,310 --> 00:13:25,520
Oh, uh, I'm sorry,
it's just a habit.

233
00:13:25,810 --> 00:13:27,900
Muslims will only eat animals

234
00:13:28,020 --> 00:13:30,360
if their throats
have been cut open first, right?

235
00:13:30,480 --> 00:13:32,650
-Yes.
-But if you do it that way,

236
00:13:32,780 --> 00:13:34,950
you just spill blood
all over the ground.

237
00:13:35,070 --> 00:13:37,950
And draining the blood
makes the meat lose its flavor,

238
00:13:38,070 --> 00:13:40,490
so then you're stuck
eating a bland-tasting meal.

239
00:13:41,030 --> 00:13:43,250
Anyway, we do things
differently here,

240
00:13:43,370 --> 00:13:44,710
so try to put up with us.

241
00:13:44,830 --> 00:13:47,920
Oh, don't worry.
I've already gotten used to it.

242
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:51,040
I've lived in Mongolia
for eight years now.

243
00:13:51,170 --> 00:13:53,460
I've even come to enjoy eating
unbled meat.

244
00:13:53,590 --> 00:13:54,470
Really?

245
00:13:55,300 --> 00:13:56,880
People who prefer
the taste of meat

246
00:13:57,010 --> 00:13:58,380
that's already been bled

247
00:13:58,510 --> 00:13:59,640
remind me of the sort of people

248
00:13:59,760 --> 00:14:01,760
who prefer sweets
that don't taste too sweet.

249
00:14:01,890 --> 00:14:05,600
I know. Well, you have
entrails to clean.

250
00:14:05,730 --> 00:14:07,390
Thank you, Fatima.

251
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:09,230
Of course, my pleasure.

252
00:14:09,350 --> 00:14:10,650
♪

253
00:14:13,400 --> 00:14:14,900
[SITARA]
There's actually a good reason

254
00:14:15,030 --> 00:14:18,030
behind butchering an animal
by cutting its throat first.

255
00:14:19,030 --> 00:14:22,580
In the name of Allah,
and Allah is the greatest.

256
00:14:23,160 --> 00:14:25,200
-[slashes]
-[gasps, whimpers]

257
00:14:25,330 --> 00:14:26,540
[ZUMURRUD] It's all right.

258
00:14:26,660 --> 00:14:28,750
That's the most painless method
for the animal.

259
00:14:29,170 --> 00:14:31,170
If the meat
has been drained first,

260
00:14:31,290 --> 00:14:35,050
then it's a much nicer color,
and it doesn't spoil as fast.

261
00:14:35,510 --> 00:14:37,260
♪

262
00:14:38,970 --> 00:14:40,010
[SITARA] Still...

263
00:14:40,130 --> 00:14:41,220
it's no wonder

264
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:43,350
I've gotten used to dark meat
that hasn't been bled.

265
00:14:44,970 --> 00:14:46,390
Eight years...

266
00:14:46,520 --> 00:14:48,690
That means I've been
living out here in Mongolia

267
00:14:49,060 --> 00:14:51,730
as many years
as I was in Tus.

268
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:58,110
And yet, after all this time,
I haven't accomplished anything.

269
00:14:58,240 --> 00:14:59,200
That book...

270
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:03,120
it's been within my grasp
for years now,

271
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:05,490
but I still haven't
taken it back.

272
00:15:06,080 --> 00:15:08,830
One could hardly say
that I've reclaimed it.

273
00:15:12,710 --> 00:15:13,750
Oh...

274
00:15:14,290 --> 00:15:15,920
There's something hard in here.

275
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:20,550
[gasps]

276
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:23,350
Could this be...

277
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:26,600
[MAN 1] Here. [grunts]
Take this one as well.

278
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:27,680
[MAN 2] Hm.

279
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:32,610
It's so strange.
I just can't believe it's him.

280
00:15:32,730 --> 00:15:33,730
Right?

281
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:36,610
[MAN] That's enough.
Today's a day for celebration.

282
00:15:36,730 --> 00:15:38,610
♪

283
00:15:38,740 --> 00:15:42,240
This is the day our
new emperor's taking the throne.

284
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:48,500
[exclaims]

285
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:54,710
Ahh!

286
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:03,800
[gasps]

287
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:09,480
[exlaiming]

288
00:16:12,690 --> 00:16:14,230
Instead of using "Khan,"

289
00:16:14,350 --> 00:16:16,320
the new emperor's
calling himself the "Kha'an."

290
00:16:16,440 --> 00:16:18,940
So he's choosing
to bring back an ancient title

291
00:16:19,070 --> 00:16:21,400
that even Genghis Khan
didn't adopt.

292
00:16:21,530 --> 00:16:23,860
The Mongols have risen
to true greatness.

293
00:16:23,990 --> 00:16:25,070
It's a new world,

294
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,700
and Mongolia will soon be
right at the center of it.

295
00:16:27,830 --> 00:16:29,450
[♪ festive music playing]

296
00:16:38,250 --> 00:16:39,550
[both grunt]

297
00:16:41,470 --> 00:16:43,260
-[all cheering]
-[grunts]

298
00:16:46,510 --> 00:16:50,100
As of right now, the Kurultai
has entered its forty-first day.

299
00:16:50,220 --> 00:16:52,310
I guess they must really be
at loggerheads then.

300
00:16:52,430 --> 00:16:54,310
The number forty-one
holds more meaning

301
00:16:54,440 --> 00:16:55,600
than you may be aware of.

302
00:16:56,150 --> 00:16:58,400
Khan's prophecy
said the forty-first day

303
00:16:58,520 --> 00:16:59,940
would be
quite an auspicious one.

304
00:17:00,440 --> 00:17:04,200
I think the prince is about
to be nominated by the clan.

305
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:05,870
That means today...

306
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:08,330
he'll take the throne.

307
00:17:10,660 --> 00:17:12,500
Onward, Great Kha'an.

308
00:17:13,290 --> 00:17:15,540
-This way.
-Now our hands will lead you.

309
00:17:15,670 --> 00:17:16,670
GENGHIS KHAN'S YOUNGER BROTHER
TEMÜGE

310
00:17:16,790 --> 00:17:17,750
SECOND PRINCE
CHAGATAI

311
00:17:20,590 --> 00:17:22,050
♪

312
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:46,820
[BOTH]
Long live the new emperor!

313
00:17:46,910 --> 00:17:49,450
[ALL]
Long live the new emperor!

314
00:17:49,570 --> 00:17:52,450
Long live Ögedei Kha'an!

315
00:17:52,910 --> 00:17:55,250
Huzzah!

316
00:17:55,370 --> 00:17:57,670
[ALL] Huzzah!

317
00:17:58,290 --> 00:18:00,750
Huzzah!

318
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:03,130
Huzzah!

319
00:18:03,250 --> 00:18:04,460
[Ögedei chuckles softly]

320
00:18:05,010 --> 00:18:06,170
[TOLUI] Great Kha'an!

321
00:18:06,760 --> 00:18:09,850
Today, I must heartily
congratulate you.

322
00:18:10,470 --> 00:18:13,020
Bravo, my brother Ögedei.

323
00:18:13,430 --> 00:18:15,270
Thank you, Tolui.

324
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:17,100
♪

325
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,920
Someday, from my bloodline,

326
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:42,250
there may be those who,
if rolled in grass,

327
00:18:42,380 --> 00:18:43,800
wouldn't be eaten by a cow,

328
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:46,460
nor eaten by a dog
if rolled in fat.

329
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:53,390
Faced with an elk
emerging crosswise,

330
00:18:53,510 --> 00:18:56,060
and a mouse emerging lengthwise,

331
00:18:56,180 --> 00:18:58,730
they are sure to let both flee.

332
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:04,690
Now, is it time for celebrating?

333
00:19:04,820 --> 00:19:06,940
My father's will
is to be carried out,

334
00:19:07,070 --> 00:19:09,320
and I'm free
of governing duties.

335
00:19:10,570 --> 00:19:11,700
Ahh!

336
00:19:11,820 --> 00:19:14,200
You did well filling in
all this time.

337
00:19:14,530 --> 00:19:15,830
Sorghaghtani...

338
00:19:16,450 --> 00:19:18,200
the only true regret I have

339
00:19:18,330 --> 00:19:20,160
is knowing
I couldn't make you empress.

340
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:21,790
Oh, don't say that.

341
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:24,800
I mean, when Father
shared his will with us,

342
00:19:24,920 --> 00:19:26,090
I couldn't help but think,

343
00:19:26,630 --> 00:19:29,630
"Why? Shouldn't it
have been me instead?"

344
00:19:29,760 --> 00:19:31,550
But this is how he explained it.

345
00:19:31,970 --> 00:19:34,810
"When a many-headed snake
tries to enter a burrow

346
00:19:34,930 --> 00:19:37,970
to outlast the cold,
the heads fight each other,

347
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:40,730
and it soon dies
without making it inside.

348
00:19:41,020 --> 00:19:43,230
Conversely, a serpent
with one head

349
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:45,730
will burrow inside
and easily survive."

350
00:19:46,270 --> 00:19:50,320
"Ögedei, use your brains
to become the head for us all."

351
00:19:50,530 --> 00:19:51,860
[exclaims]

352
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:54,910
Being the Otchigin,

353
00:19:55,030 --> 00:19:57,790
I began to assume he favored me
over the others.

354
00:19:58,330 --> 00:20:01,410
But no, that isn't what
Father was thinking at all.

355
00:20:01,910 --> 00:20:04,290
The great power
he bestowed upon me

356
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:06,250
wasn't simply for me alone.

357
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:09,420
There's one thing that will make
the Mongols strong,

358
00:20:09,550 --> 00:20:12,010
and it's the bond we share
as brothers.

359
00:20:12,130 --> 00:20:15,220
That is what my father,
Genghis Khan,

360
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:17,010
wished for.

361
00:20:17,140 --> 00:20:19,180
It is my greatest wish as well.

362
00:20:22,770 --> 00:20:24,770
[SORGHAGHTANI]
Your brotherly bond.

363
00:20:32,990 --> 00:20:34,360
[Sitara sighs]

364
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:37,280
It doesn't matter to me
which one of the brothers

365
00:20:37,410 --> 00:20:39,490
sits on the throne
as the emperor.

366
00:20:39,950 --> 00:20:43,370
But breaking years of tradition
just to have him succeed you?

367
00:20:43,500 --> 00:20:46,840
Prince Ögedei couldn't possibly
be more qualified.

368
00:20:48,920 --> 00:20:50,300
[chuckles]

369
00:20:50,420 --> 00:20:52,420
Seems Shira
backed the wrong horse.

370
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:59,010
In any case, the Kurultai can
finally come to an end now.

371
00:21:00,100 --> 00:21:01,430
[gasps]

372
00:21:06,020 --> 00:21:09,270
Is this stone
truly what I think it is?

373
00:21:09,400 --> 00:21:11,650
I read about it in
one of my mistress's books.

374
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:13,530
It's extremely valuable.

375
00:21:13,650 --> 00:21:14,950
[SORGHAGHTANI] Fatima?

376
00:21:15,070 --> 00:21:16,990
[SITARA] Princess Sorghaghtani?

377
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:23,830
[SITARA] Uh, what's the matter?

378
00:21:25,040 --> 00:21:27,460
I have something important
to discuss.

379
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:28,500
With me?

380
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:30,170
After tonight,

381
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:33,090
I no longer want you
to be by my side anymore.

382
00:21:33,880 --> 00:21:36,970
Wait... What?
How could this be?

383
00:21:37,090 --> 00:21:39,180
You think I've done
something wrong, is that it?

384
00:21:39,300 --> 00:21:40,720
It is nothing like that at all.

385
00:21:40,850 --> 00:21:42,560
Then what could it be?

386
00:21:44,730 --> 00:21:45,980
[Sitara grunts]

387
00:21:46,890 --> 00:21:48,020
Hmm?

388
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:51,520
Fatima, I want you...

389
00:21:53,860 --> 00:21:56,610
to act as a spy for me.

390
00:21:57,110 --> 00:21:58,530
[Sitara gasps]

391
00:22:02,450 --> 00:22:05,160
[♪ closing theme song playing]

392
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:34,790
[SITARA (ADULT)] Next time,
"A Snake Shows Its Colors.

393
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:36,880
Man Hides His Colors."

